{"comparisons":[],"failures":[],"frontier":[],"initial":{"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines private market assets and direct and indirect exposure routes.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u1.5"},{"reason":"Defines Funds and management-company scope; distinguishes disclosure duties from possible classification.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u4.564"},{"reason":"Explains classification risk considerations without establishing an independent trigger.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u7.1028"},{"reason":"Investor information and distributor selection expectations do not independently determine classification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u10.1937"},{"reason":"Disclosure section heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u11.2466"},{"reason":"Potential exposure triggers disclosure guidance, not automatic complex-product classification.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u14.2516"},{"reason":"Disclosure of exposure extent and access may support classification assessment; illustrative percentages supply no actual classification evidence.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u15.2718"},{"reason":"Underlying asset disclosures may support exposure assessment.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u16.2995"},{"reason":"Risk disclosure requirements remain distinct from the classification trigger.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u17.3223"},{"reason":"Identifies the classification section.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u18.3743"},{"reason":"Establishes the inclusive 50% mandatory threshold and additional discretionary designation route.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779"},{"reason":"Aggregate exposure is a discretionary assessment factor.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u22.4078"},{"reason":"Strategy, composition, liquidity and risk inform discretionary assessment.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u24.4176"},{"reason":"Asset characteristics inform discretionary assessment; no automatic tranche or rating trigger is supplied.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u26.4290"},{"reason":"Home-regulator conditions are factors, not stated automatic classification rules.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u28.4505"},{"reason":"Requires holistic assessment of discretionary designation.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u29.4630"},{"reason":"Classification engages prevailing complex-product sales requirements, including suitability irrespective of solicitation or recommendation.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u32.4805"},{"reason":"Target-market and distributor-selection section heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u33.5086"},{"reason":"Separate product-approval requirements are incorporated by reference; their full content is absent.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u36.5149"},{"reason":"Managers should choose distributors with knowledge of the Fund, including its complex-product status; this does not grant distributors the SFC's designation discretion.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u39.5617"},{"reason":"Advertising obligations are separate from classification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u42.6275"},{"reason":"Section heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u43.6653"},{"reason":"Closer authorisation scrutiny and possible FASTrack exclusion are distinct from complex-product classification.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u46.6668"},{"reason":"Existing funds require review and appropriate action as soon as practicable; consultation is encouraged where classification is doubtful.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955"},{"reason":"Identifies a clarification route, not a classification condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u52.7565"},{"reason":"Issuing division identification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u55.7698"},{"reason":"Issuing institution identification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u56.7736"},{"reason":"The separate 15% direct-investment limit does not replace the 50% aggregate classification threshold; UT Code details are unavailable.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u58.7778"},{"reason":"Indirect exposure examples are expressly non-exhaustive and may be updated.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u59.7979"},{"reason":"Defines BDCs for the exposure examples.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u60.8163"},{"reason":"Defines CLOs for the exposure examples.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u61.8338"},{"reason":"Provides derivative exposure examples, including TRSs and SRTs.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u62.8487"},{"reason":"Excludes LAFs from the defined Funds and directs them to a separate circular whose rules are unavailable.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"},{"reason":"Attaches the below-50% qualification to holistic discretionary assessment, not to the mandatory threshold.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"},{"reason":"Identifies external sales requirements; their complete content and relevant FAQs are absent.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u65.9044"},{"reason":"Dates concern the referenced product-approval circular, not commencement of this circular.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u66.9304"},{"reason":"April 2013 concerns the referenced advertising guidelines, not commencement of this circular.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u67.9509"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"Classification concerns funds authorised for public offering in Hong Kong, excluding LAFs. Guidance addresses managers; SFC discretion and the resulting distribution obligations have distinct actors.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u32.4805","d4148dd852cee.u39.5617"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Private market assets comprise private credit and private equity. Direct and indirect exposures aggregate, with non-exhaustive indirect examples. The strongest unresolved issue is how instrument positions translate into measured exposure: the packet does not specify look-through, netting, leverage, double counting or valuation conventions.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u1.5","d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u59.7979","d4148dd852cee.u60.8163","d4148dd852cee.u61.8338","d4148dd852cee.u62.8487"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The LAF exclusion attaches to the defined Funds. Below 50% is not an exemption from designation: footnote 7 identifies the domain of holistic discretionary assessment. The 15% direct-investment limit is a separate constraint.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910","d4148dd852cee.u58.7778"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"At least 50% entails classification; below that threshold the SFC may designate case by case. Risk factors do not themselves establish a designation. Disclosure, distributor selection, authorisation scrutiny and encouraged consultation have separate modalities and triggers.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u22.4078","d4148dd852cee.u24.4176","d4148dd852cee.u26.4290","d4148dd852cee.u28.4505","d4148dd852cee.u46.6668","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"No commencement date, measurement frequency, threshold-breach duration or declassification rule is supplied. Existing-fund actions are expected as soon as practicable. Dates attached to external documents do not establish this circular's effective date.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955","d4148dd852cee.u66.9304","d4148dd852cee.u67.9509"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The LAF circular, UT Code, sales codes and FAQs, product-approval circular and advertising guidelines are referenced but not supplied. Three missing dependency identifiers have no source hashes or mapping to particular references. Full downstream duties and external classification grounds cannot be resolved.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u58.7778","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u65.9044","d4148dd852cee.u36.5149","d4148dd852cee.u66.9304","d4148dd852cee.u42.6275","d4148dd852cee.u67.9509"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["What exposure-calculation methodology applies to BDCs, CLOs, TRSs and SRTs, including look-through, leverage, netting and avoidance of double counting?","Does the threshold use current holdings, permitted maximum exposure or another measure, and at what valuation and assessment times?","What commencement, transition, monitoring and declassification rules apply?","For the particular Fund, what evidence establishes its scope, measured aggregate exposure and any operative SFC designation?","Which referenced documents correspond to missing.7b393f53d503773a762cf757, missing.de6722b4a9f08d782e48c11a and missing.13ee048eabca24d91ac9305c, and what relevant provisions do they contain?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["This proposal evaluates only the retained circular's classification routes for one Fund at a specified assessment time.","The circular is applicable at that assessment time; the packet does not establish commencement.","The threshold fact must be supplied using a supported exposure methodology, not inferred from illustrative holdings or disclosure language.","An operative SFC designation requires evidence of an actual designation; risk factors or the possibility of designation are insufficient.","Unknown scope, exposure or designation facts remain unknown. Absence of designation evidence is not evidence of no designation."],"citations":[{"quote":"funds that are authorised by the SFC for offering to the public in Hong Kong (Funds)6","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u4.564"},{"quote":"6 Except for listed closed-ended alternative asset funds (LAFs).","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"},{"quote":"A Fund will be considered as a complex product if its total direct and indirect exposures to private market assets amount to 50% or more of the Fund’s NAV.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779"},{"quote":"On a case-by-case basis, the SFC may also designate a Fund as a complex product, taking into account factors including, without limitation:","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779"},{"quote":"the SFC will adopt a holistic approach taking into account the specific circumstances of the case.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u29.4630"},{"quote":"In cases where the Fund’s aggregate direct and indirect exposures to private market assets are less than 50% of the Fund’s NAV.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"},{"quote":"including but not limited to ensuring the suitability of the Fund for its investors irrespective of whether solicitation or recommendation is involved.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u32.4805"},{"quote":"Fund managers are encouraged to consult the SFC at the earliest opportunity if they are in doubt regarding complex product classification of their Funds.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955"}],"distinction":"The substantive distinction is automatic classification at the inclusive 50% threshold versus an actual discretionary SFC designation below it. Neither private-market exposure alone nor an adverse risk factor automatically establishes classification. LAF exclusion removes this circular's route without establishing that a LAF is non-complex under other rules. The text supports this single classification reading more strongly than competing automatic-classification rules; uncertainty chiefly concerns measurement, timing and missing evidence.","family":"modality","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"Whether the assessed fund is authorised by the SFC for offering to the public in Hong Kong at the assessment time.","name":"public_sfc_authorised","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the assessed fund is a listed closed-ended alternative asset fund within the footnote 6 exclusion.","name":"is_laf","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the Fund's total direct and indirect exposure to private market assets amounts to at least 50% of its NAV at the assessment time, using the applicable methodology. Missing or unresolved measurement evidence leaves this fact unknown.","name":"aggregate_exposure_at_least_half_nav","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u1.5","d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u59.7979"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether an SFC case-by-case designation of this Fund as a complex product under this circular is operative at the assessment time. Mere designation risk or missing records does not establish either truth value.","name":"operative_sfc_designation","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(or aggregate_exposure_at_least_half_nav operative_sfc_designation)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and public_sfc_authorised (not is_laf))"},"local_id":"classification_routes","questions":["How is aggregate exposure measured and evidenced for the Fund at the relevant time?","Is there an actual operative SFC designation, rather than only circumstances that could justify one?","If exposure subsequently falls below 50%, what rules govern continued classification?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Selected control: whether the retained circular's complex-product classification trigger is satisfied for an in-scope Fund at the assessment time. True means aggregate direct and indirect private-market exposure reaches at least 50% of NAV, or an operative SFC case-by-case designation exists, so the Fund must be treated as complex for distribution under this reading. False means both routes are affirmatively absent; it does not establish general non-complex status, compliance with sales duties or exemption under other instruments. An out-of-scope Fund receives no classification decision from this control. Missing evidence remains unresolved rather than producing false.","subject":"Complex-product classification trigger for an SFC-authorised public Fund, excluding LAFs"}]}},"java_checks":[],"live_provider":true,"model_calls":2,"no_progress":0,"nodes":[],"pending":"action.959c9c89f6454fc08203b87df2bbbe2a","provider_id":"codex.fresh.v1.compact.v2","retrievals":[],"rounds":0,"roundtrips":[],"run_id":"run.07ade899f13b40218b344b2eaeb2295c","stop":null}